run 11 - 2026-09-01 - run 10 got the editor BUILT and the cook actually
running: 32 seconds inside UnrealEditor-Cmd before Error_UnknownCookFailure.
The reason was above the 40-line tail, which is the cap-biting-silently
fault in my own instrument, so error lines are now pulled from the whole
cook log with both caps announced. Two hypotheses ride this run. The cook
has no content to cook, so MapsToCook points at an engine map that
certainly exists, which tests the cook path without inventing a binary
asset. And the game module never reaches StartupModule at all: the
breadcrumb has come back absent on every run since it was added, so the
package-loader crash happens BEFORE Default-phase module loading. The
module moves to PostConfigInit. That is a deliberate gamble: UE may refuse
a non-Default phase for a primary game module, and if it does it will say
so plainly and cost one round trip.
